course: dictionary
lesson: 9959
title: Taurus, the bull in the sky
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Taurus is a word with more than one meaning, so context tells you which one is meant. In a science lesson, Taurus is a constellation: a group of stars that looks like a shape in the night sky. «Taurus has the V-shaped Hyades and the Pleiades» talks about stars, so it is the sky meaning.
explain: The clue words are «stars», «winter evenings» and «north». A constellation is not a real animal, even though its shape looks like one. Taurus is Latin for bull, which is why people imagine a bull in those stars.
explain: Taurus can mean other things too. In astrology it is a star sign for people born from about late April to late May. A name for mountains in Turkey, or a product such as a car, is not about stars at all. Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence before you decide.
fact: A constellation is a group of stars that looks like a shape.
fact: Taurus is Latin for «bull».
fact: The bright star Aldebaran is orange, and it is in Taurus.
fact: «Taurus has the V-shaped Hyades and the Pleiades.»
fact: Astrology uses star signs, but science teaches that astrology is not a science.
exercise: A constellation called Taurus looks like which animal? | *A bull | A hunter | A crab | A pair of twins
exercise: «Orion's belt points up-right to orange Aldebaran in Taurus.» What colour is Aldebaran? | Blue | *Orange | Green | White
exercise: Taurus is the Latin word for which animal? | Lion | *Bull | Hunter | Twin
test: «In 1054 Chinese astronomers recorded a guest star, and its remains are the Crab Nebula in Taurus.» In which group of stars is the Crab Nebula? | *Taurus | Orion | Sirius | Gemini
test: Someone says Taurus is a star sign that tells the future, so it must be a science. What is the right answer? | Taurus is a car, so it is science | *Astrology is not a science, but a star sign is a group of people's birthdays | Stars never have names | Yes, astrology is a science
exam: «Orion's belt points down-left to Sirius, the brightest star, and up-right to orange Aldebaran in Taurus.» Which star in Taurus is orange? | Castor | Pollux | Sirius | *Aldebaran
